+## Findings, ranked
+
+### FINDING #1 — INTEGRATION_MISMATCH · the same seam one layer downstream · made reachable by `2aef342`
+
+**Every external worker copies `scope` verbatim out of the slice into
+`job_result.tests.scope`, where `schemas/job_result.schema.json` declares a three-value enum and
+the value is now a fourth.**
+
+The copy is direct and unconditional:
+
+```
+scripts/compound-v-run-codex-worker.sh:174   _tc_scope=$(jq -r '.scope' "$_tc_f")
+scripts/compound-v-run-codex-worker.sh:207   --arg scope "$_tc_scope" \
+scripts/compound-v-run-codex-worker.sh:216        scope: $scope,
+```
+
+against
+
+```
+schemas/job_result.schema.json:107-113
+  "scope": { "type": "string", "enum": ["full", "impacted", "floor_only"] }
+```
+
+Reproduced on the real slice from the sandbox above:
+
+```bash
+jq -r .scope "$SB/slice-scoped.json"
+# impacted+referencing
+jq -c '.properties.tests.properties.scope.enum' schemas/job_result.schema.json
+# ["full","impacted","floor_only"]
+# membership → 'impacted+referencing' in enum? False
+```
+
+The same three lines exist in all five workers (`grep -n "_tc_scope"
+scripts/compound-v-run-*-worker.sh`).
+
+**Why this is `2aef342`'s to own, even though the schema is older.** Before the fix the worker died
+at `tc_validate` (exit 2) and never reached the reporting block, so the out-of-enum value could not
+be produced. The fix removed the thing that was stopping it. That is precisely the shape of
+review-2's #1 — a producer and a consumer wired together with nobody having run one into the other
+— advanced by one joint.
+
+**Honest severity.** No runtime path rejects it *today*:
+`compound-v-collect-results.py:381-440`'s conformance checker is top-level-only (required keys,
+`additionalProperties`, top-level types, plus a targeted `usage` sub-check); it never walks into
+`tests`, and no other script enforces the enum. So it does not crash a run now. It is a published
+contract the producer violates, in a repository that dispatches Claude jobs and so would never
+notice — the exact blind spot that let review-2's #1 live through two passes.
+
+**And the label is currently emittable nowhere legally.** The native path filters it out:
+
+```
+scripts/compound-v-emit-workflow.py:3195   TESTS_SCOPES = ("full", "impacted", "floor_only")
+scripts/compound-v-emit-workflow.py:3231   for candidate in ((contract or {}).get("scope"), (job or {}).get("test_scope")):
+                                             if isinstance(candidate, str) and candidate in TESTS_SCOPES:
+```
+
+so a native job silently falls back to the job's declared `test_scope`. Meanwhile
+`agents/spec-reviewer.md:190` instructs the reviewer that `tests.scope` "additionally carries the
+output-only label `impacted+referencing`". Three components, three answers: the schema forbids it,
+the native emitter drops it, the reviewer contract says to read it.
+
+→ Pick one and make all three obey it. Adding `"impacted+referencing"` to the schema enum and to
+`TESTS_SCOPES` is one line each and matches the reviewer contract already shipped; the alternative
+is to have the workers normalise the label back to `impacted` on the way into `tests.scope` and
+delete the sentence at `spec-reviewer.md:190`. Do not leave it as it is — a schema is worth only
+what its producers honour.
+
